WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.840
Breaking into the spotlight as Sarah Connor
in James Cameron's classic film The Terminator,

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.440
Linda Hamilton became a pop culture icon.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:12.900
Since reprising her role in 1991's Terminator
2, she's been less visible — but it turns

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.380
out, she never really stepped away from the
spotlight.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.920
Where's she been all these years?

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.840
Let's take a look at what Linda Hamilton's
been up to since joining the battle to take

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.720
down Skynet.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.360
Small screen

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.420
After The Terminator, Hamilton turned her
attention back to television, appearing in

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:33.120
the series Hill Street Blues, as well as TV
movies Club Med and Go Toward the Light.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.300
In 1987, she stepped into the role of Catherine
Chandler on CBS's Beauty and the Beast.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.880
The series earned multiple accolades during
its three-year run, including a Best Actor

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.580
Golden Globe for Hamilton's co-star Ron Perlman.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:50.380
She hit her stride with big-screen success
in films like Mr. Destiny and Dante's Peak,

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.260
and then continued to jump back and forth
between film and television.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:59.270
Starting in the late '90s, Hamilton guest-starred
in shows like Frasier, According to Jim, and

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:02.680
Weeds, as well as a three-episode arc on the
Syfy series Lost Girl.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:08.219
In 2010, the quirky NBC action procedural
Chuck got some extra star power when Hamilton

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.440
joined the cast to play a former CIA agent
— and Chuck's sinister spy mother.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.380
A shipwrecked marriage

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.200
For a brief period, Hamilton was married to
the man that helped her become Sarah Connor:

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.460
director James Cameron.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:25.780
After Cameron split with his third wife, director
Kathryn Bigelow, he and Hamilton connected.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:32.719
In 1993, she gave birth to their daughter,
Josephine, and from 1997 to 1999, the two

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.180
were officially husband and wife.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.639
As Hamilton told The Daily Mail, Cameron wasn't
someone who could easily settle down.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.240
She explained,

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.560
"The woman he can't get is always his dream
girl.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.540
Work and women go hand in hand for Jimbo,
and I should know."

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.880
Cameron and Hamilton split when he fell in
love with actress-turned-environmental advocate

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:54.580
Suzy Amis, who he met on the set of Titanic,
resulting in a $50 million divorce settlement.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.500
A mental health battle

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:02.380
In a 2005 interview with Larry King, Hamilton
spoke openly about her ongoing struggles with

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:07.059
bipolar disorder, saying that after multiple
mistreatments, she'd finally been able to

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.380
get the appropriate care to manage the illness.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.640
According to Hamilton, the emotional swings
associated with the condition are one of the

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:16.080
main reasons her first two marriages came
to an end.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.360
Hamilton explained,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.340
"I really want to stress that there is no
magic pill for everyone...

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.680
I've got this huge busy brain.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.880
I need to go and sweat for an hour and do
my weights for half an hour or an hour, not

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:26.480
every day.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.860
It's no longer the compulsion, but I just
know that that helps me feel better."

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:35.500
"I like to speak out to let people know that
they're not alone at feeling control at times."

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.219
A meaningful role

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:43.980
In 2014, the Syfy network debuted Defiance,
a high-concept series released in tandem with

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.520
a video game of the same name.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.140
Hamilton joined the cast for a six-episode
arc as a woman who suffered from mental illness

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:55.109
and lost access to medication after the arrival
of aliens, causing violent outbursts against

00:02:55.109 --> 00:02:55.700
her family.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:00.080
The series lasted only three seasons, but
it gave Hamilton an outlet to help educate

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:03.489
audiences about mental illness, an important
personal issue for her.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:05.580
Discussing her character, she told TV Guide,

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:09.760
"Pilar is a fantastic character — manic,
mad and full of secrets.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.240
This is why I love doing sci-fi.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.840
You can go to so many more interesting places
than you can in some forensic cop drama."

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.740
Heard but not seen

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.100
While Hamilton has worked regularly, a lot
of the roles she's performed haven't been

00:03:22.109 --> 00:03:26.550
in front of the camera — instead, her distinctive
voice has helped bring life to a variety of

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:27.760
animated characters.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:32.359
She's become a mainstay in the DC animated
universe, where she's lent her voice to projects

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:36.960
such as The New Batman Adventures, Batman
Beyond, and a number of DC Showcase short

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:37.460
films.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.420
Hamilton told Animation World Network,

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.740
"This form of creating a character is backwards
from what I'm used to, in that they start

00:03:43.749 --> 00:03:46.790
with the script and your voice, and then create
around that.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.180
It's a very different way of acting."

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.080
She'll be back

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.019
It's been more than 25 years since Hamilton
last appeared in Terminator 2, and in the

00:03:55.019 --> 00:03:59.920
meantime, there have been a number of installments
in the Terminator franchise — 2003's Rise

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.109
of the Machines, 2008's short-lived TV series
Terminator: The Sarah Connor Chronicles, 2009's

00:04:05.109 --> 00:04:09.480
Terminator Salvation, and 2015's Terminator
Genisys.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:13.760
Now, according to Deadline, Cameron is getting
the band back together for a new trilogy.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.220
"I've been waiting for you"

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:21.380
Reportedly, the next installment will ignore
the timeline explored in the sequels that

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:25.860
came after T2, and Arnold Schwarzenegger and
Hamilton will both reprise their roles.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.920
Discussing Hamilton's return, Cameron said,

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:32.460
"As meaningful as she was to gender and action
stars everywhere back then, it's going to

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.920
make a huge statement to have that seasoned
warrior that she's become return.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.760
There are 50-year-old, 60-year-old guys out
there killing bad guys, but there isn't an

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.100
example of that for women."

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:45.080
Linda Hamilton is definitely back — and
it sounds like she's better than ever.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.640
"He said there's a storm coming in"

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:53.220
"I know."

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:54.600
Thanks for watching!

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:57.580
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.879
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

